<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tiananmen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1420">1420</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Gate of Heavenly Peace</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tiananmen, the Gate of Heavenly Peace, is the monumental gate at the southern entrance to the Imperial City of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a>, first built in 1420 under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming dynasty</a> and rebuilt in 1651. From its rostrum <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mao-zedong">Mao Zedong</a> proclaimed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China</a> on 1 October 1949, and with his portrait it became a national emblem, overlooking Tiananmen Square.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tiananmen.jpg" alt="Tiananmen" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Balon Greyjoy · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:20200110_Tiananmen-3.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
